<!--
  Custom decoders for the Wazuh manager.
  Path on the manager: /var/ossec/etc/decoders/local_decoder.xml

  cowrie-json
    On Wazuh 4.14 a clean Cowrie JSON line came back "No decoder matched" in
    wazuh-logtest and fell to rule 1002. The prematch pins Cowrie lines by
    their opening eventid and hands them to the JSON plugin, so the fields
    (eventid, src_ip, username, input...) get extracted.
    Without the plugin_decoder line Wazuh recognises the line but extracts
    nothing, which looked like "decoding complete" with no fields under it.

  Things I tried and dropped, so nobody repeats them:
    - A child decoder with <parent>json</parent> plus its own regex, to rename
      Heralding's reserved "protocol" field. It replaced the parent's whole
      field set instead of adding one field (known Wazuh issue). Heralding
      rules match destination_port now.
    - A dedicated prematch decoder for ConPot Guardian AST. The real fix was
      chaining the rules onto built-in rule 86600.
    - A regex decoder to clean Dionaea's flattened FTP command array. The live
      rule 100076 uses pcre2 word boundaries instead. Also learned that
      plugin_decoder and regex cannot sit in the same decoder block, and that
      decoder regex needs type="pcre2" for capture groups.
-->
<decoder name="cowrie-json">
  <prematch>^{"eventid":"cowrie\.</prematch>
  <plugin_decoder>JSON_Decoder</plugin_decoder>
</decoder>
